roducts for tires, such as high-reinforcing grades and semi-reinforcing grades under the ECORAX brand, as well as for mechanical rubber goods end users, including automotive production, construction, as well as certain food, consumer, and medical applications. It operates in the United States, Brazil, rest of the Americas, Germany, South Africa, Italy, Spain, Czech republic, Poland, Italy, Turkey, France, Rest of EMEA, China, the Republic of Korea, and rest of Asia. The company was formerly known as Orion Engineered Carbons S.A. and changed its name to Orion S.A. in June 2023. Orion S.A. was founded in 1862 and is headquartered in Senningerberg, Luxembourg.","ceo_bio":"Mr. Corning F. Painter | CEO & Executive Director | Age 63 | Compensation: $1.8M (FY2025)","culture_narrative":"Employs approximately 1K people. Revenue per employee of $1.1M ranks in the top quartile among Basic Materials peers. Each employee generates $33K of free cash flow annually. Stock-based compensation of $8K per employee reflects an ownership culture. CEO compensation is 2\u00d7 revenue per employee (modest relative to workforce productivity). Governance score flags moderate compensation governance risk (4/10).","financial_summary":["Orion S.A. is a micro-cap basic materials business with a $225M market cap on $1.8B of annual revenue.","The top line has compounded at -4% over the past three years, and a shrinking top line is the hardest headwind any business can overcome.","Returns on capital run at 10% against a 8% cost of capital, which means the business barely earns its keep economically, and 24% gross margins are typical of commodity economics where competitors can replicate the product cheaply.","The business throws off $55M in free cash flow \u2014 roughly 3 cents on every revenue dollar, which is the owner-earnings figure that actually belongs to shareholders.","On the balance sheet, debt is heavy at 5.8\u00d7 net debt/EBITDA, and leverage like that is what turns a bad year into a permanent loss, and thin 0.5\u00d7 interest coverage leaves no room for a bad year.","Management returns a meaningful 13.1% of market cap to owners through dividends and buybacks, a strong signal of disciplined capital allocation, and insiders hold 3.9% of the shares, and profit capture is only 0.1\u00d7 the fair share, suggesting no structural edge inside its industry."],"sector_headwinds":[{"text":"Piotroski score 3/9 \u2014 the fundamentals are deteriorating on multiple fronts","sev":"red","cat":"quality"},{"text":"Altman Z in the distress zone (1.4) \u2014 the kind of balance-sheet risk that can make a loss permanent","sev":"red","cat":"quality"},{"text":"Low reinvestment-driven growth suggests the compounding engine has stalled","sev":"amber","cat":"growth"},{"text":"Operating margins softening -1.6pp YoY \u2014 early warning on the moat","sev":"amber","cat":"trend"},{"text":"Fragmented industry with below-average profit capture \u2014 no moat to protect margins","sev":"amber","cat":"moat"},{"text":"Volatile returns on capital suggest the moat is narrower than a snapshot ROIC implies","sev":"amber","cat":"moat"},{"text":"Value-trap profile (score 57/100): leveraged balance sheet under pressure; roic below cost of capital \u2014 cheapness may reflect deterioration, not mispricing","sev":"amber","cat":"value_trap"},{"text":"Carries more leverage than most Basic Materials peers \u2014 a smaller cushion for the inevitable bad year","sev":"amber","cat":"balance_sheet"},{"text":"Weakness in commodity prices pressures materials companies","sev":"amber","cat":"sector"},{"text":"Trade policy and tariff whiplash \u2014 materials producers are first-order casualties of protectionist swings, and margin gets squeezed from both input and output pricing.","sev":"amber","cat":"thesis_risk"}],"sector_tailwinds":["Trading at a 81% margin of safety to estimated fair value \u2014 a real cushion against errors in the estimate","Market is pricing in lower growth than the company has historically delivered","Trading near the bottom of its 52-week range \u2014 the market is offering a discount","Valued at a 28% discount to sector median EV/EBITDA","Healthy payout ratio leaves room for both dividend growth and reinvestment"],"news_headlines":[{"title":"SpaceX launches Starship on ambitious 22-hour Flight 15 test, but aborts booster 'chopsticks' catch (video)","source":"space.com","link":"https://www.space.com/space-exploration/launches-spacecraft/spacex-starship-flight-15-chopsticks-double-catch-super-heavy-ship","date":"2026-11-13","timestamp":1794612003.0,"origin":"tiingo","sentiment":0.392,"tier":2,"scope":"company","tags":["product"]},{"title":"Orion Group: 3 Key Takeaways for Long-Term Investors","source":"finance.yahoo.com","link":"https://finance.yahoo.com/markets/stocks/articles/orion-group-3-key-takeaways-222002710.html","date":"2026-11-13","timestamp":1794608402.0,"origin":"tiingo","sentiment":0.25,"tier":2,"scope":"company","tags":[]},{"title":"NASA is looking for new astronauts; do you have what it takes?","source":"aol.com","link":"https://www.aol.com/articles/nasa-looking-astronauts-takes-200008000.html","date":"2026-11-13","timestamp":1794602618.0,"origin":"tiingo","sentiment":0.382,"tier":2,"scope":"company","tags":[]},{"title":"SpaceX to attempt double catch of huge Starship rocket","source":"aol.com","link":"https://www.aol.com/articles/spacex-attempt-double-catch-huge-201207000.html","date":"2026-11-13","timestamp":1794601537.0,"origin":"tiingo","sentiment":0.318,"tier":2,"scope":"company","tags":[]},{"title":"Elon Musk\u2019s SpaceX to attempt double catch of Starship rocket","source":"bbc.co.uk","link":"https://www.bbc.co.uk/news/articles/ckregdgnl0xpo","date":"2026-11-13","timestamp":1794600722.0,"origin":"tiingo","sentiment":0.0,"tier":2,"scope":"company","tags":[]},{"title":"Think you have good eyesight? Try counting the stars in the Pleiades tonight","source":"space.com","link":"https://www.space.com/stargazing/think-you-hav